[38;5;252m[1m## What I found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust code compiled cleanly on the first [38;5;10mcargo build --release[0m, so all the work was behavioral. Three real divergences:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m1. Uninitialized stack buffers.[22m A [38;5;10mscanf[0m [3mmatching[23m failure returns 0, not [38;5;10mEOF[0m, so the C loop does not [38;5;10mbreak[0m — it [38;5;10mstrcpy[0ms a buffer the failed conversion never touched. On iteration 2+ that's the previous record's value (which the translation already modeled), but on iteration 1 it's raw stack garbage. The reference [38;5;10m-O0[0m build reproducibly leaves [38;5;10mluggage_id == "\x03"[0m, so stdin like [38;5;10mabc\n[0m printed [38;5;10m0000000000 \x03    abc[0m from C and [38;5;10m0000000000     abc[0m from Rust. This is genuine UB — the garbage changes at [38;5;10m-O1[0m/[38;5;10m-O2[0m/[38;5;10m-O3[0m/[38;5;10m-Os[0m — but it's rock-stable for the build [38;5;10mCMakeLists.txt[0m produces (200 runs, varied argv length, [38;5;10menv -i[0m, 3 KB env var), so I reproduce it behind a named constant and flag the caveat.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m2. [38;5;10mstrcpy[0m NUL truncation.[22m [38;5;10m%80[^\n][0m stores a NUL byte read from stdin and counts it against the 80-char width, but the following [38;5;10mstrcpy[0m stops there. [38;5;10m5 LUG1 FL1 JFK LAX ab\0cd\n[0m gave [38;5;10mab[0m from C and [38;5;10mab\0cd[0m from Rust. Fixed by truncating at store time — not scan time, since the post-NUL bytes still determine where the next conversion starts.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m3. [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m.[22m Rust's runtime sets [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m; C inherits the default. Piping into [38;5;10mhead[0m gave status 141 from C and 0 from Rust. Fixed with a [38;5;10msignal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL)[0m call at startup.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Confirmed identical without changes: [38;5;10m%d[0m-into-[38;5;10munsigned int[0m clamping and truncation (including a 10 000-digit input), the per-[38;5;10mscanf[0m EOF exits, the dropped final record when a trailing newline is absent, the double space before comments, field-width spill-over, the [38;5;10msupersedes()[0m first-match-wins quirk, and the [38;5;10mmatches()[0m wildcard rules.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
