[0m[0m
[38;5;10mtranslation/tests/differential.rs[0m — 36 tests, ~1900 argv/stdin combinations, all driving both binaries as subprocesses and comparing stdout, stderr and exit status. Nothing ignored or skipped; passes in both debug and release. The harness rebuilds [38;5;10mc_src/build/driver[0m with CMake if it's missing, which I verified by deleting it and re-running. Separately, ~85 000 randomized inputs through an out-of-tree fuzzer with zero mismatches.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One divergence I documented rather than fixed: the C recursion in [38;5;10maddRoutingDirectiveToList[0m/[38;5;10msupersedes[0m would overflow an 8 MiB stack near 175 000 directives where the iterative Rust would not — but reaching that depth also costs Θ(n²) in [38;5;10mprintMatchingDirectives[0m, so it needs hours of CPU before it could crash. [38;5;10mc_src/[0m is unmodified (hashes and mtimes unchanged); only the [38;5;10mbuild/[0m directory CMake creates was added.[0m[0m
